zephyr (1.4.0) testing; urgency=medium

  * Add `zfr about`, `zfr version`, and `zfr lint` (and
    zfr-about / zfr-version / zfr-lint wrappers). Each walks
    from the current directory to the project root (meson project() or
    debian/control).
  * `zfr version` prefers git describe when git and .git exist, else
    debian/changelog, then a VERSION file, then 0.0.0. `-r` maps hyphens
    to underscores for RPM. Meson and rpm/Makefile call `zfr` on PATH
    and fall back to VERSION (not a relative tools/zfr path).
  * `zfr about` prints parsed common fields from debian or RPM
    (section, priority, distribution, architecture, and so on) wrapped
    to the terminal, plus source file/line counts and an estimated
    payload size. `-d`/`-r` reformat packaging metadata rather than
    dumping files. CSR colors on a TTY.
  * `zfr lint` checks packaging and layout against zephyr style
    (missing files, identity, Meson/Debian/RPM, leftover template
    tokens) and prints coded findings with fixes. CSR colors on a TTY.
  * Snapshot the changelog version in VERSION (allowed to differ from
    git describe). .githooks/pre-commit syncs VERSION from
    debian/changelog; `zfr create` sets git core.hooksPath to
    .githooks.
  * Add parent rpm/ packaging (Meson, noarch, aligned with
    debian/control). Track rpm/*.spec. `zfr create` copies the
    VERSION pre-commit hook into new projects.
  * Refactor bash RPM packaging to match debian/control (Meson, noarch,
    AGPL-3.0-or-later, bash-shlib).
  * Add `zfr dist` (and zfr-dist). Uses `meson dist` when the
    project is the git root (`--allow-dirty`, `--no-tests` by default);
    nested language templates pack only that directory. Prints the
    archive path on stdout. rpm/Makefile `dist` and the Meson `srcdist`
    ninja target call this command.
  * Apply the same versioning and RPM layout to the remaining language
    templates (not only bash). meson.build uses `zfr version`, then
    VERSION, then 0.0.0. Each language ships rpm/zephyr.spec aligned
    with debian/control (dynamic %{version}, Meson, AGPL) and
    rpm/Makefile calling `zfr dist --rpm`.
  * Add `zfr ize` (and zfr-ize). In-place upgrade of an existing
    project to current zephyr style: missing debian/rpm files from the
    language template, VERSION and pre-commit hook, meson.build patches
    (`zfr version`, asciidoctor man targets, `look`, completions),
    groff `.1` → `docs/*.adoc`, and hardcoded src versions → `@VERSION@`
    / `config.h`. `-n` dry-run. Then `zfr lint`.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 01:33:00 +0800

